1. **What did you learn about handling user input in this activity?**
   Users rarely type data in a neat, consistent format—they might accidentally add extra spaces or use all lowercase letters. Using string methods like `.strip()`, `.title()`, and `.upper()` ensures the final output looks professional regardless of how messy the input is.
2. **How did using the `datetime` module improve your program?**
   Instead of just printing raw numbers separated by slashes, `datetime` allowed me to convert numeric inputs into a proper date object and format it with `strftime()` so the month name is spelled out clearly.
3. **Why is version control (GitHub) useful when building programs?**
   Saving the project in three separate versions helped me build the program step-by-step. Starting with basic inputs and outputs made it easier to test my logic before adding string formatting and date handling, and it gives a clear history of how the code improved over time.

